{
  "_documentation": "Dated operating-system end-of-life table used by the intune.device_os_end_of_life rule. Auditex reads it from configs/ and never from the network. verified_on is the date every entry was last checked against its sources; refresh the table (and verified_on) when a release is added or a date changes, and keep tests/test_os_lifecycle.py green. end_of_support is the last day the vendor serves security updates for every General Availability edition of the release; a device is past end of life only after that date. end_of_support_home_pro is the earlier date for Home and Pro editions when it differs: between the two dates the edition decides, and Intune's osVersion does not show it, so the rule reports unknown (edition_dependent) rather than guess. ltsc_end_of_support is the last day of the latest Long-Term Servicing release that shares the build (LTSC, LTSB or IoT Enterprise LTSC): osVersion does not show the edition, so between end_of_support and ltsc_end_of_support the state is unknown (edition_dependent), and only after ltsc_end_of_support is the build past end of life. Windows Server shares some builds and is not covered. extended_support_until is a paid extension (Windows 10 ESU) whose enrolment Auditex cannot see. end_of_support is null while the vendor still patches the release. A release that is not in the table, or a version that cannot be parsed, is unknown, never supported. confidence is vendor_published for dates the vendor publishes and derived for Apple and Android, which publish none.",
  "schema_version": "2026-10-22",
  "verified_on": "2026-10-22",
